## Conversation
User asked to prove the new cuda-12.9 entry end to end on GB300 (driver runs
older userspace fine); first build attempt died in deepgemm-builder.

## Actions
Probed on a GB300 pod with the cu12.9 base image: (1) trivial kernel at
-arch=sm_103a compiles under nvcc 12.9 (the load-bearing B300 assumption);
(2) mqa_logits.cuh compiles under nvcc bare, FAILS under host g++ bare,
passes under g++ with -include cuda_fp8.h. Upstream fork main already deleted
the __nv_fp8_e4m3 usage. Fixed via sed in the downloader + DEEPGEMM_SRC_DIR
for the vendored build; verified deepgemm.cmake normalizes absolute paths and
hard-fails on a missing dir.

## Errors & Mistakes
First probe cloned without submodules (--filter=tree:0), so both variants
failed on cutlass/arch/barrier.h and looked inconclusive; second probe with
submodules gave the clean split.

## Dead Ends
Bumping DEEPGEMM_COMMIT past the upstream refactor instead: rejected because
vLLM's deepgemm.cmake pins f5a76426 for the vendored copy, and the wheel must
match it (the shadowing rule) -- a newer wheel over an older vendored copy
recreates the original K3 TypeError class.

## Hints for Future Agents
The DEEPGEMM_SRC_DIR mount also removes a mid-build network fetch from
vllm-builder; if the vendored build ever needs a writable source tree it will
fail loudly on the read-only bind mount. The sed targets line 3's barrier.h
include; if the pin moves, the grep guard fails the build rather than
silently skipping.

## Codebase Discoveries
CUDA 13 header chains include cuda_fp8.h transitively where 12.9's do not --
expect this class of failure in any cu13-era CUDA code first built on 12.9.

